    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and tested. Here's what was wrong and how I fixed it:\n\n## Summary\n\n**The Bug:**\nThe `frai` CLI program had a `--ci` option defined at the program level. When you ran `frai gate init --ci`, Commander.js was parsing the `--ci` flag at the program level before routing to the `gate` subcommand. This meant the `args` passed to the gate handler only contained `['init']` without the `--ci` flag, so the workflow file creation code was never executed.\n\n**The Fix:**\nI made two changes to `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`:\n\n1. **Line 604**: Added `.enablePositionalOptions()` to the program initialization to properly support options in subcommands\n2. **Line 742**: Added `.passThroughOptions(true)` to the `gate` command to ensure options defined at the program level are passed through to the subcommand\n\n**Verification:**\n\u2705 Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n\u2705 Tested `frai gate init --ci` in a clean directory\n\u2705 Both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are now correctly created\n\u2705 The workflow file has the proper GitHub Actions configuration\n\nThe bug is now fixed!",
